Maintainer repair is now on public head `d0e1b43e724b6887a4444577f7559ae1c2495571`.

This resolves the outstanding [ClawSweeper P1](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/123874#issuecomment-5299149311):

- shipped Browser/Desktop `open: true` state seeds only the current otherwise-fresh session layout, once;
- an existing per-session layout remains authoritative;
- unrelated later sessions remain closed;
- shipped `open: false` state creates no tab (explicit negative-control regression test);
- route-startup Browser/Desktop/Terminal intents now retain one owner through the shell-to-pane handoff, and embedded panels no longer write standalone dock geometry/visibility.

Focused proof: migration 3/3, Discussion-panel 9/9, ownership/migration suite 36/36 on the repaired tree, focused tabbed-panel E2E pass, UI build/size budgets pass, autoreview clean, and independent source-blind C1/C2/C3 validation pass. Hosted exact-head CI is running now and remains the landing authority for current-main merge-ref coverage.

The green video was recorded at product parent `cce0ef9b461`; public head `d0e1b43e724` has the identical product tree plus the `open: false` test-only negative control.

Base — independent rails:

https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b5082ad5-2f71-4b7c-856b-bedd8fe1f299

Head — unified tabbed side panel:

https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/95f53885-6ef7-4abc-88db-1bf364d33190

@clawsweeper re-review

Follow-up CI repair is now on exact public head `17e9de5bb96d0c17d3e849162ac32d58e8952c53`.

- removed the test-only exported Desktop host type flagged by dead-code CI;
- collapsed the embedded Browser startup to one snapshot and fenced viewport resize until a successful view exists, so failed media fetches no longer recapture-loop;
- kept explicit Terminal catalog intent dominant over later mount-time restore intent, preventing the post-service-worker duplicate open;
- scoped the service-worker assertion to the embedded Terminal owner.

Focused reruns pass: Browser failed-body E2E 1/1, service-worker Terminal restore E2E 1/1, the two previously timing-failed Claude-session cases 2/2, Browser/Terminal unit suites 117/117, dependency export scan 0 findings, max-lines ratchet, typed Oxlint, and autoreview clean (0.99). The previously posted raw base/head videos remain the user-visible proof; this follow-up changes lifecycle correctness only.

@clawsweeper re-review
